BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seattle 48 Hour Film Project Premiere Screenings 2025
DTSTART:20250722T013000Z
DTEND:20250722T035000Z
DTSTAMP:20250722T013000Z
UID:dFZuODco65
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nPresented by Create 48 Media Net
 work The Seattle 48 Hour Film Project is an annual competition where filmm
 akers create a short film in just 48 hours. Celebrating it’s 20th year i
 n 2025\, this event fosters creativity and community among Washington’s 
 vibrant filmmaking talent. Participants draw a genre from a hat\, and must
  incorporate specific elements such as a character\, prop\, and line of di
 alogue into their films. The resulting short films are screened at SIFF Ci
 nema Uptown\, with the top film advancing to Filmapalooza 2026 in Lisbon\,
  Portugal\, and a chance to be featured at the Cannes Film Festival 2026. 
 Join us for a weekend of creativity\, teamwork\, and cinematic magic! Pass
 es: $72 ($48 Members)Individual Tickets: $18 ($10 Members\, Students\, Se
 niors\, and Veterans)\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/seattle-4
 8-hour-film-project-premiere-screenings-2025
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
